      "text": "Given the complex numbers \\( z \\) that satisfy both \\( z^{28} - z^8 - 1 = 0 \\) and \\( |z| = 1 \\), we start by dividing the equation by \\( z^8 \\) to get:\n\n\\[ z^{20} - 1 - \\frac{1}{z^8} = 0 \\]\n\nSince \\( |z| = 1 \\), we can write \\( z = e^{i\\theta} \\). Substituting \\( z = e^{i\\theta} \\) into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[ (e^{i\\theta})^{20} - 1 - \\frac{1}{(e^{i\\theta})^8} = 0 \\]\n\\[ e^{20i\\theta} - 1 - e^{-8i\\theta} = 0 \\]\n\\[ e^{20i\\theta} - 1 = e^{-8i\\theta} \\]\n\nLet \\( w = e^{i\\theta} \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[ w^{20} - 1 = w^{-8} \\]\n\\[ w^{20} = w^{-8} + 1 \\]\n\\[ w^{20} - w^{-8} = 1 \\]\n\nThis equation is satisfied by \\( w = e^{i\\alpha} \\) where \\( \\alpha \\) is such that \\( w^{20} = w^{-8} + 1 \\). We need to find the values of \\( \\alpha \\) that satisfy this equation. The solutions to this equation are the arguments of the roots of a polynomial. By Euler's formula, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[ e^{20i\\theta} - 1 = e^{-8i\\theta} \\]\n\\[ e^{20i\\theta} - e^{-8i\\theta} = 1 \\]\n\\[ 2i \\sin(12\\theta) = 1 \\]\n\\[ \\sin(12\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2i} \\]\n\\[ \\sin(12\\theta) = -\\frac{i}{2} \\]\n\\[ \\cos(12\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nThe solutions to \\( \\cos(12\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2} \\) are:\n\n\\[ 12\\theta = 60^\\circ + 360^\\circ k \\]\n\\[ \\theta = 5^\\circ + 30^\\circ k \\]\n\nFor \\( 0 \\leq \\theta < 360 \\), the possible values of \\( \\theta \\) are:\n\n\\[ \\theta = 5^\\circ, 35^\\circ, 65^\\circ, 95^\\circ, 125^\\circ, 155^\\circ, 185^\\circ, 215^\\circ, 245^\\circ, 275^\\circ, 305^\\circ, 335^\\circ \\]\n\nThese are the angles \\( \\theta_m \\) in degrees. We need to find the sum \\( \\theta_2 + \\theta_4 + \\dots + \\theta_{2n} \\). The even-indexed angles are:\n\n\\[ \\theta_2 = 35^\\circ, \\theta_4 = 95^\\circ, \\theta_6 = 155^\\circ, \\theta_8 = 215^\\circ, \\theta_{10} = 275^\\circ, \\theta_{12} = 335^\\circ \\]\n\nThus, the sum is:\n\n\\[ \\theta_2 + \\theta_4 + \\theta_6 + \\theta_8 + \\theta_{10} + \\theta_{12} = 35^\\circ + 95^\\circ + 155^\\circ + 215^\\circ + 275^\\circ + 335^\\circ \\]\n\\[ = 1075^\\circ \\]\n\nTherefore, the value is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{1075} \\]",
