      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given equation \\(z^{28} - z^8 - 1 = 0\\) and the magnitude condition \\(|z| = 1\\). Let \\(z = e^{i\\theta}\\), where \\(\\theta = \\alpha + 2k\\pi\\) for \\(k = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots, 27\\). Substituting \\(z = e^{i\\alpha}\\) into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n(e^{i\\alpha})^{28} - (e^{i\\alpha})^8 - 1 = 0 \\implies e^{28i\\alpha} - e^{8i\\alpha} - 1 = 0.\n\\]\n\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\ne^{8i\\alpha}(e^{20i\\alpha} - 1) = 1.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(|e^{8i\\alpha}| = 1\\), the equation holds true if \\(e^{20i\\alpha} = 1\\). This means \\(20\\alpha = \\frac{2k\\pi}{2} = \\frac{k\\pi}{2}\\) for \\(k = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots, 9\\). Therefore, \\(\\alpha = \\frac{k\\pi}{20}\\) for \\(k = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots, 8\\). The angles \\(\\alpha\\) range from \\(0\\) to \\(8\\) radians, and since \\(0 \\leq \\theta_m < 360\\) degrees, we convert \\(\\alpha\\) from radians to degrees:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{180k}{20} = 9k^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the angles \\(\\theta_m\\) are \\(9, 18, 27, 36, 45, 54, 63, 72, 81, 90, 99, 108, 117, 126, 135, 144, 153, 162, 171, 180\\). We need to find the value of \\(\\theta_2 + \\theta_4 + \\dots + \\theta_{2n}\\). Notice that the angles \\(\\theta_m\\) form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(9\\) and the common difference \\(18\\). We need to find the sum of the terms \\(\\theta_2 + \\theta_4 + \\dots + \\theta_{2n}\\), which is the sum of the terms of the sequence starting at \\(18\\) with a common difference of \\(36\\):\n\n\\[\n18, 54, 90, \\ldots, 2(9 + (2n-2) \\cdot 18) = 18, 54, 90, \\ldots, 18(1 + (n-1) \\cdot 2) = 18(1 + 2n-2) = 18(2n-1).\n\\]\n\nThe number of terms in this sequence is \\(\\frac{2n-1}{2} + 1 = n\\). The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum} = \\frac{n}{2} (2 \\cdot 9 + (n-1) \\cdot 36) = \\frac{n}{2} (18 + 36n - 36) = \\frac{n}{2} (36n - 18) = 9n(2n - 1).\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\theta_2 + \\theta_4 + \\dots + \\theta_{2n}\\) is \\(\\boxed{9n(2n-1)}\\).",
