      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start by analyzing the equation \\(z^{28} - z^8 - 1 = 0\\). Let \\(z = e^{i\\theta}\\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n(e^{i\\theta})^{28} - (e^{i\\theta})^8 - 1 = 0 \\implies e^{28i\\theta} - e^{8i\\theta} - 1 = 0.\n\\]\n\nWe can rewrite this as:\n\n\\[\ne^{8i\\theta}(e^{16i\\theta} - 1) - 1 = 0 \\implies e^{16i\\theta}(e^{8i\\theta} - e^{16i\\theta}) = -1.\n\\]\n\nLet \\(w = e^{8i\\theta}\\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\nw^2 (w - w^2) = -1 \\implies w^3 - w^4 = -1 \\implies w^4 - w^3 + 1 = 0.\n\\]\n\nThe solutions to the equation \\(w^4 - w^3 + 1 = 0\\) are the fourth roots of unity, but excluding the roots that would make \\(w = e^{i\\theta}\\) a fourth root of unity (which would imply \\(\\theta = 0, 90, 180, 270\\) modulo 360). The fourth roots of unity are \\(1, -\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i, -\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i, -1\\). However, since \\(w = e^{8i\\theta}\\) and \\(|w| = 1\\), the valid solutions are \\(w = -1, \\omega, \\omega^2, \\omega^3\\) where \\(\\omega = e^{2i\\pi/3} = -\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i\\).\n\nThis means \\(e^{8i\\theta} = -1, \\omega, \\omega^2, \\omega^3\\), so \\(8\\theta = 180^\\circ, 240^\\circ, 300^\\circ, 360^\\circ\\) modulo \\(360^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\theta = 22.5^\\circ, 30^\\circ, 37.5^\\circ, 45^\\circ\\).\n\nThe angles \\(\\theta_1, \\theta_2, \\ldots, \\theta_{2n}\\) are \\(0^\\circ, 22.5^\\circ, 30^\\circ, 37.5^\\circ, 45^\\circ, 52.5^\\circ, 60^\\circ, 67.5^\\circ\\). The sum of the angles is:\n\n\\[\n0^\\circ + 22.5^\\circ + 30^\\circ + 37.5^\\circ + 45^\\circ + 52.5^\\circ + 60^\\circ + 67.5^\\circ = 330^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe problem asks for the sum of the angles \\(2\\theta_2 + 4\\theta_4 + 6\\theta_6 + \\cdots + 2n\\theta_{2n}\\). Using the sum of the angles and knowing that the indices are even, we get:\n\n\\[\n2(22.5) + 4(30) + 6(37.5) + 8(45) + 10(52.5) + 12(60) + 14(67.5) + 16(75) = 45 + 120 + 225 + 360 + 525 + 1200 + 882 + 1200 = 4937.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\theta_2 + \\theta_4 + \\cdots + \\theta_{2n}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4937}\\).",
